<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Leo III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/750">750</a>–816 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Leo III crowned</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Leo III was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from 795 to 816. On Christmas Day 800 CE he crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Emperor of the Romans</a> in St Peter's Basilica. The coronation established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>'s imperial title and was later regarded as the origin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii.jpg" alt="Pope Leo III" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Various: Original: Unknown author Restoration: Ferdinando Fuga (1743) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pope_Leo_III_portrait_%E2%80%93_Triclinium_Leoninum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
